{
  "case_id": "2008-07-610",
  "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case addresses whether the First and Fourteenth Amendments permit public employers to compel nonunion employees to subsidize the union's expressive speech of a political nature in a public forum, specifically litigation in courts and before administrative agencies not involving their bargaining unit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But, of course, they wouldn't be subsidizing it if -- if, indeed, it is some kind of a -- essentially an insurance scheme."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Obviously First Amendment harm, Justice Kennedy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But why isn't litigation -- what I don't understand is how you draw a line between the -- the negotiation of an agreement, where Lehnert said this kind of pooling is okay, and the enforcement of the agreement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Young",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YOUNG: For the -- I'm sorry, Justice Ginsburg. For the agreement, for the unit, we concede that the union may charge for that public speech of a political nature in a public forum. We have no dispute over charging for enforcing or -- or -- enforcing the collective bargaining agreement. That is not our dispute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: You have several times mentioned the public forum as having a significance in drawing the line and I'm not sure I follow you there. Why did you say that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So we are talking\nabout an infringement on the objecting members' first\namendment rights, and your answer is trust us, we'll\ntreat you fairly? I understand that it's a different\nanswer if you say you've got a right. We can impose the\ncontribution requirement on you, even though you object\nto it because under this agreement, you have a right to\ncall upon our services. That's a different case. But\nif your answer is simply trust us we'll treat you\nfairly, that's not the usual standard we apply to\ninfringements of First Amendment rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: The issue is not whether\nthat's a fair thing for the national union to do. The\nissue is whether the person who is being compelled\nagainst his will to pay dues to the union is getting\nanything back for that compelled payment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If certain -- if certain\nfees are are being assessed on the theory that this is a\npooling arrangement, I don't understand why you're\nresisting any effort to impose any standards or any\ninquiry as to whether it's really a pooling arrangement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is there a rule or a reg\nsomewhere in the Labor Department that says if the\nnational union takes its money from its local, spends it\nin a way that has nothing to do with politics\nwhatsoever, zero -- but either wastes it or they build\ntoo big a building, or they do something that doesn't\nbenefit Local Number 432, does 432 have any remedy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Collins",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84d575e04a9-0002-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. COLLINS: There is no Labor Department\nregulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-610",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "e84d575e04a94e201256e30c3f58fbe42b0e25e687bb84caafb416ef36d8a58d",
